{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><strong><i><u>(Note: Playing this game requires a certain understanding of Chinese idioms. If you are completely unfamiliar with this, the author suggests that you do not try this game easily.)</u></i></strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">&quot;The Story of Pie Na&quot; is a simple game that combines&quot; filling idioms &quot;and&quot; walking in a maze &quot;.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">And on this basis, different game mechanisms are added to enhance players' enjoyment in the game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3715490/extras/83b66a4c-06ec-4c84-a6af-e3e2f1948c9f.png?t=1747149052\" /></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Players will take on the role of a human who has fallen to a different realm, constantly advancing or retreating through &quot;filling in idioms&quot; in order to return to their hometown.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">In the process of understanding and comprehending traditional idioms, players can also play the role of a &quot;traveler&quot;, &quot;ranger&quot;, and &quot;wanderer&quot; who travels through the world, listening to the stories of each character in the game and deciding whether to get involved, making choices that they will not regret.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3715490/extras/0541189a-9041-40f2-8890-dbe05ad97c30.png?t=1747149052\" /></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Can you hold onto your inner choice until you reach the end of your journey?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Those seemingly settled things are quietly undergoing changes.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p 